  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nاِقْرَاْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَۚ‏(1)\nIQRAA BISME RABBEKAL LAZEE KHALAQ.\nRead in the name of your Lord Who created. \nخَلَقَ الْاِنْسَانَ مِنْ عَلَقٍۚ‏(2)\nKHALAQAL INSAANA MIN A’LAQ.\nHe created man from a clot. \nاِقْرَاْ وَرَبُّكَ الْاَكْرَمُۙ‏(3)\nIQRAA WA RABBOKAL AKRAMUL.\nRead and your Lord is Most Honorable, \nالَّذِىْ عَلَّمَ بِالْقَلَمِۙ‏(4)\nLAZEE A’LLAMA BIL-QALAME.\nWho taught (to write) with the pen \nعَلَّمَ الْاِنْسَانَ مَا لَمْ يَعْلَمْؕ‏(5)\nA’LLAMAL INSAANA MAA LAM YA’LAM.\nTaught man what he knew not. \nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ لَيَطْغٰٓىۙ‏(6)\nKALLAA INNAL INSAANA LA-YATGHAA.\nNay! man is most surely inordinate, \nاَنْ رَّاٰهُ اسْتَغْنٰىؕ‏(7)\nAR RA-AAHUS TAGHNAA.\nBecause he sees himself free from want. \nاِنَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ الرُّجْعٰىؕ‏(8)\nINNA ELAA RABBEKAR RUJ-A’A.\nSurely to your Lord is the return. \nاَرَءَيْتَ الَّذِىْ يَنْهٰىؕ‏(9)\nA-RA-AYTAL LAZEE YANHAA.\nHave you seen him who forbids \nعَبْدًا اِذَا صَلّٰىؕ‏(10)\nA’BDAN EZAA SALLAA.\nA servant when he prays? \nاَرَءَيْتَ اِنْ كَانَ عَلَى الْهُدٰٓىۙ‏(11)\nA-RA-AYTA IN KAANA A’LAL HODAA.\nHave you considered if he were on the right way, \nاَوْ اَمَرَ بِالتَّقْوٰىۙ‏(12)\nAW AMARA BIT-TAQWAA.\nOr enjoined guarding (against evil)? \nاَرَءَيْتَ اِنْ كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلّٰىؕ‏(13)\nA-RA-AYTA IN KAZZABA WA TAWALLAA.\nHave you considered if he gives the lie to the truth and turns (his) back? \nاَلَمْ يَعْلَمْ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَرٰىؕ‏(14)\nALAM YA’LAM BE-ANNAL LAAHA YARAA.\nDoes he not know that Allah does see? \nكَلَّا لَئِنْ لَّمْ يَنْتَهِ ۙ لَنَسْفَعًۢا بِالنَّاصِيَةِۙ‏(15)\nKALLAA LA-IL LAM YANTAHE, LA-NASFA-A’M BIN-NAASEYATE.\nNay! if he desist not, We would certainly smite his forehead, \nنَاصِيَةٍ كَاذِبَةٍ خَاطِئَةٍ ۚ‏(16)\nNAASEYATIN KAAZEBATIN KHAATE-ATAH.\nA lying, sinful forehead. \nفَلْيَدْعُ نَادِيَهٗ ۙ‏(17)\nFAL-YAD-O’ NAADEYAHU.\nThen let him summon his council, \nسَنَدْعُ الزَّبَانِيَةَ ۙ‏(18)\nSA-NAD-U’Z ZABAANEYATAH.\nWe too would summon the braves of the army. \nكَلَّا ؕ لَا تُطِعْهُ وَاسْجُدْ وَاقْتَرِبْ۩‏(19)\nKALLAA, LAA TO-TE’HO WAS-JUD WAQ TARIB.\nNay! obey him not, and make obeisance and draw nigh (to Allah).",
  "merits": "Surah al-Alaq (The Clot)\nThere are 19 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that whoever recites this Surah in the daytime or at night, and then passes away, he will be counted amongst the martyrs who died while fighting on the side of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.).\nIt is highly recommended to recite this Surah while travelling and it acts as a safety from accidents. If recited on a treasure, it remains safe."
